    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Four players in fixed partnerships, as at short whist. No card is turned for trumps. After the deal the dealer may declare a suit for trumps or say pass, in which case the partner must declare. The declarer may instead say biritch (no trumps). After declaration either adversary may say contre (doubles trick values); the dealer side may say sur contre (quadruples), and doubling may continue until one side stops. The player to the left of the dealer leads. The dealer's partner then exposes all cards as Dummy, played by the dealer; Dummy may not suggest plays. Revokes and misdeals as at short whist. A game is 30 points in play; honours do not count toward the game. Best of three games wins the rubber.",
    Player: "Four players in fixed partnerships, as at short whist. No card is turned for trumps. After the deal the dealer may declare a suit for trumps or say pass, in which case the partner must declare. The declarer may instead say biritch (no trumps). After declaration either adversary may say contre (doubles trick values); the dealer side may say sur contre (quadruples), and doubling may continue until one side stops. The player to the left of the dealer leads. The dealer's partner then exposes all cards as Dummy, played by the dealer; Dummy may not suggest plays. Revokes and misdeals as at short whist. A game is 30 points in play; honours do not count toward the game. Best of three games wins the rubber.",
    objective: 'Win tricks with your partnership. The first side to score 30 points in play wins a game. Best of three games (a rubber) wins the rubber.',
    gameplay: "Four players in fixed partnerships, as at short whist. No card is turned for trumps. After the deal the dealer may declare a suit for trumps or say pass, in which case the partner must declare. The declarer may instead say biritch (no trumps). After declaration either adversary may say contre (doubles trick values); the dealer side may say sur contre (quadruples), and doubling may continue until one side stops. The player to the left of the dealer leads. The dealer's partner then exposes all cards as Dummy, played by the dealer; Dummy may not suggest plays. Revokes and misdeals as at short whist. A game is 30 points in play; honours do not count toward the game. Best of three games wins the rubber.",
    keyRules: [
      'Dealer (or partner) declares trumps â€” no card turned up. Revolutionary departure from Whist.',
      "'Biritch' = no-trump declaration. The origin of the word 'Bridge.'",
      'Dummy hand is exposed and played by the dealer.',
      'Contre/sur-contre doubles/quadruples trick values infinitely.',
      '30 points wins a game. Best of 3 games wins the rubber.',
      'Honours score separately and do not affect games.',
    ],
