    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 13 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win tricks with your partnership. The first side to score 30 points in play wins a game. Best of three games (a rubber) wins the rubber.',
      "Turn-flow example: Four players in fixed partnerships, as at short whist. No card is turned for trumps. After the deal the dealer may declare a suit for trumps or say pass, in which case the partner must declare. The declarer may instead say biritch (no trumps). After declaration either adversary may say contre (doubles trick values); the dealer side may say sur contre (quadruples), and doubling may continue until one side stops. The player to the left of the dealer leads. The dealer's partner then exposes all cards as Dummy, played by the dealer; Dummy may not suggest plays. Revokes and misdeals as at short whist. A game is 30 points in play; honours do not count toward the game. Best of three games wins the rubber.",
      'Scoring example: Odd tricks (above 6) count toward game score. 30 points = one game. Best 2 of 3 games = rubber. Honours scored separately. First side to win 2 games wins the rubber..',
